From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: realign the EL queue at the moment of pairing

amdv_parse_metadata_v2_stb() pairs each base-layer frame with whatever is at the
head of the dvel queue; FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS is off and the slave EL carries no pts
(pts_us64 == 0 on every EL frame, measured), so position is the only identity.
Any BL that leaves without its EL leaves that EL at the head, and every later
composite would use the wrong one.

The vendor keeps the queues in step in recv_common_dequeue_frame()
(video_receiver.c): the decoders' vf_put_count totals must match, and a BL
surplus is a surplus of stale ELs to drop. That receiver is not on the Blu-ray
chain (dvbldec amlvideo deinterlace amvideo), so the previous version of this
patch ran the same check from the amvideo vsync before the dequeue. Two faults:

  - it sampled the totals before the unpaired BL had been put back, so after a
    0012 miss it acted one vsync late: the late EL paired with the next BL, and
    the next check then dropped that BL's own, correct EL. Each miss cost a
    BL-only frame, a mispaired frame and a destroyed EL (FEL_test fv.dbg.dmesg).
  - amvideo_vf_put() skipped amdv_vf_put() while amdv was disabled, so a BL
    put during a DV mode switch or display reset left its EL in the dv_vf table
    uncounted, and the check then retired a correct queued EL (EL ahead for the
    rest of the title). On multi_dv_mode the table is never reclaimed at session
    end either ("multi-mode todo").

The check now runs inside the parse, just before dvel_vf_get(), and adds the
term the totals cannot see yet: BLs shown without their EL (0012 misses) that
are still held - on screen or awaiting an RDMA-deferred put. A miss therefore
costs exactly one BL-only frame. The routes the totals do cover are kept - above
all a BL the player returns undisplayed, which amlvideo puts straight back to
the decoder and which never reaches the parse (M3GAN 2.0: every start-of-feature
"surplus" line matches a Kodi ReleaseFrame drop to the millisecond).

Only ELs already queued are retired; nothing waits for an EL or takes one ahead
of its BL. The held-miss list is kept apart from the dv_vf table, because a BL in
that table is never parsed again and a still that missed must still be able to
take its late EL. A BL whose EL the decoder produced but amdv bypassed is held
the same way (its EL is owed, and the queue keeps draining while the bypass
lasts); after BLs for which the decoder produced no EL the count restarts,
excluding those still on screen, and a new EL receiver registration takes the decoders'
totals at that moment as its baseline. amvideo_vf_put() now returns the EL
before the BL, so the EL total never trails the BL total mid-put. On
multi_dv_mode (S6) dvel unregistration now also clears the EL-bearing dv_inst
entries it left behind ("multi-mode todo"), so a reused BL address in the next
session cannot carry a stale EL into the new EL decoder.

Known limit, shared with the vendor check and the version this replaces: a BL
the player drops while an earlier BL is still queued for display is counted
before that earlier BL is paired, so one frame can take the next EL before the
queue settles. dvel_miss_count and dvel_retire_count
(/sys/module/aml_media/parameters/) count BL-only frames and retired ELs.

Signed-off-by: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
---
diff -ru a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c	2026-09-27 21:35:17.817737099 -0400
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c	2026-09-27 22:23:04.619743945 -0400
@@ -2208,6 +2208,197 @@
 	return vf;
 }
 
+/* Keep the EL queue in step with the BL, the way the vendor does it in
+ * recv_common_dequeue_frame() (video_receiver.c): every BL the decoder has
+ * taken back must have had its EL taken back too, so a surplus of BL returns
+ * over EL returns is a surplus of stale ELs at the head of the dvel queue.
+ *
+ * That receiver is not on the Blu-ray chain (dvbldec amlvideo deinterlace
+ * amvideo), so the check runs here, at the moment of pairing, and it adds the
+ * one term the put totals cannot see: a BL shown WITHOUT its EL (a 0012 miss)
+ * that is still on screen or waiting on an RDMA-deferred put. Its EL is owed
+ * already, but no put has said so yet - sampling the totals alone corrects one
+ * vsync late, pairs the late EL with the next BL and then retires that BL's own
+ * EL. Counting the held miss retires the late EL before the next BL pairs, so a
+ * miss costs one BL-only frame and nothing else.
+ *
+ * Routes the totals do cover: a BL the player returns undisplayed (amlvideo puts
+ * it straight back to the decoder and it never reaches this parse), and BLs
+ * toggled while amdv is disabled.
+ *
+ * Only surplus ELs that are already queued are retired: an EL is never waited
+ * for, never taken ahead of its BL, and never held here.
+ */
+#define DVEL_RETIRE_MAX 32
+static struct vframe_s *dvel_miss_bl[16];
+/* BLs for which the decoder produced no EL, not yet put back: their puts are
+ * still to come and must not count as owed ELs after a rebase.
+ */
+static struct vframe_s *dvel_noel_bl[16];
+static s32 dvel_put_base;
+static bool dvel_put_rebase;
+static unsigned int dvel_miss_count;
+module_param(dvel_miss_count, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dvel_miss_count, "BL frames composited without their EL");
+static unsigned int dvel_retire_count;
+module_param(dvel_retire_count, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dvel_retire_count, "stale EL frames retired to realign the EL queue");
+
+static bool dvel_put_count(const char *provider, u32 *count);
+
+/* A new dvel session starts even with the BL decoder: whatever the BL decoder
+ * has already returned before the EL receiver registered owes nothing here.
+ */
+static void dvel_put_baseline(void)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u32 bl_put = 0, el_put = 0;
+
+	if (!dvel_put_count("dvbldec", &bl_put) ||
+	    !dvel_put_count("dveldec", &el_put))
+		return;
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+	dvel_put_base = (s32)(bl_put - el_put);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/* caller holds amdv_lock */
+static void dvel_miss_reset_locked(void)
+{
+	memset(dvel_miss_bl, 0, sizeof(dvel_miss_bl));
+	memset(dvel_noel_bl, 0, sizeof(dvel_noel_bl));
+	dvel_put_base = 0;
+	dvel_put_rebase = false;
+}
+
+/* caller holds amdv_lock */
+static void dvel_miss_put_locked(struct vframe_s *bl)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_miss_bl); i++)
+		if (dvel_miss_bl[i] == bl)
+			dvel_miss_bl[i] = NULL;
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_noel_bl); i++)
+		if (dvel_noel_bl[i] == bl)
+			dvel_noel_bl[i] = NULL;
+}
+
+/* A BL the decoder gave no EL: nothing is owed for it, now or when it is put. */
+static void dvel_note_noel(struct vframe_s *bl)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int i, free = -1;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_noel_bl); i++) {
+		if (dvel_noel_bl[i] == bl)
+			break;
+		if (!dvel_noel_bl[i] && free < 0)
+			free = i;
+	}
+	if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_noel_bl) && free >= 0)
+		dvel_noel_bl[free] = bl;
+	dvel_put_rebase = true;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/* Record (miss) or clear (!miss) a BL shown without its EL. Kept apart from
+ * the dv_vf table on purpose: a BL in that table is never parsed again
+ * (amdv_vf_check), and a still re-toggled after a miss must still be able to
+ * pick up its late EL.
+ */
+static void dvel_note_miss(struct vframe_s *bl, bool miss, bool count)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int i, free = -1;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_miss_bl); i++) {
+		if (dvel_miss_bl[i] == bl)
+			break;
+		if (!dvel_miss_bl[i] && free < 0)
+			free = i;
+	}
+	if (!miss) {
+		if (i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_miss_bl))
+			dvel_miss_bl[i] = NULL;
+	} else if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_miss_bl)) {
+		if (free >= 0)
+			dvel_miss_bl[free] = bl;
+		if (count)
+			dvel_miss_count++;
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/* req.vf == NULL is the decoder's put-count query (vh265.c answers with
+ * atomic_read(&hevc->vf_put_count)). aux_size is seeded with a sentinel so a
+ * provider that does not answer is detected rather than read as zero.
+ */
+static bool dvel_put_count(const char *provider, u32 *count)
+{
+	struct provider_aux_req_s req;
+
+	memset(&req, 0, sizeof(req));
+	req.aux_size = 0xffffffff;
+	vf_notify_provider_by_name(provider,
+		VFRAME_EVENT_RECEIVER_GET_AUX_DATA, (void *)&req);
+	if (req.aux_size == 0xffffffff)
+		return false;
+	*count = req.aux_size;
+	return true;
+}
+
+/* bl is the BL about to be paired: if it is itself a held miss being parsed
+ * again, its EL is the one it is about to take, not a stale one.
+ */
+static void dvel_retire_owed(const char *bl_provider, struct vframe_s *bl)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u32 bl_put, el_put;
+	s32 owed;
+	int held = 0, n = 0, i;
+
+	if (!bl_provider || !dvel_put_count(bl_provider, &bl_put) ||
+	    !dvel_put_count("dveldec", &el_put))
+		return;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+	/* Coming back from BLs that were deliberately not paired (the EL was
+	 * bypassed): those BL returns are not owed ELs. Start counting afresh.
+	 */
+	if (dvel_put_rebase) {
+		int noel = 0;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_noel_bl); i++)
+			if (dvel_noel_bl[i])
+				noel++;
+		dvel_put_base = (s32)(bl_put - el_put) + noel;
+		dvel_put_rebase = false;
+	}
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dvel_miss_bl); i++)
+		if (dvel_miss_bl[i] && dvel_miss_bl[i] != bl)
+			held++;
+	owed = (s32)(bl_put - el_put) - dvel_put_base + held;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
+
+	while (owed > 0 && n < DVEL_RETIRE_MAX && dvel_vf_peek()) {
+		struct vframe_s *el = dvel_vf_get();
+
+		if (!el)
+			break;
+		dvel_vf_put(el);
+		owed--;
+		n++;
+	}
+	if (n) {
+		dvel_retire_count += n;
+		pr_info_ratelimited("dvel: bl put %u el put %u held %d - retired %d stale el\n",
+			bl_put, el_put, held, n);
+	}
+}
+
 static struct vframe_s *dv_vf[16][2];
 static void *metadata_parser;
 static bool metadata_parser_reset_flag;
@@ -2218,6 +2409,7 @@
 	unsigned long flags;
 	struct vframe_s *el_put[16];
 	int el_num = 0;
+	bool dvel_unreg_multi = false;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
 	if (vfm_path_on) {
@@ -2232,6 +2424,13 @@
 			//	dv_inst[dv_id].dv_vf[i][0] = NULL;
 			//}
 			//dv_inst[dv_id].frame_count = 0;
+			/* The EL decoder is going away: a BL still paired with one of
+			 * its ELs would otherwise keep that pointer, and a new session
+			 * reusing the BL's address would skip its parse and put the old
+			 * EL into the new EL decoder. Only EL-bearing entries belong to
+			 * this session; single-layer instances are left alone.
+			 */
+			dvel_unreg_multi = true;
 		} else {
 			for (i = 0; i < 16; i++) {
 				if (dv_vf[i][0]) {
@@ -2252,11 +2451,31 @@
 		crc_bypass_count = 0;
 		amdv_el_disable = 0;
 	}
+	dvel_miss_reset_locked();
 	vfm_path_on = false;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < el_num; i++)
 		dvel_vf_put(el_put[i]);
+
+	if (dvel_unreg_multi) {
+		int inst;
+
+		for (inst = 0; inst < NUM_INST; inst++) {
+			el_num = 0;
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+			for (i = 0; i < 16; i++) {
+				if (dv_inst[inst].dv_vf[i][1]) {
+					el_put[el_num++] = dv_inst[inst].dv_vf[i][1];
+					dv_inst[inst].dv_vf[i][0] = NULL;
+					dv_inst[inst].dv_vf[i][1] = NULL;
+				}
+			}
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
+			for (i = 0; i < el_num; i++)
+				dvel_vf_put(el_put[i]);
+		}
+	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(dv_vf_light_unreg_provider);
 
@@ -2292,6 +2511,7 @@
 		crc_bypass_count = 0;
 		amdv_el_disable = 0;
 	}
+	dvel_miss_reset_locked();
 	vfm_path_on = true;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&amdv_lock, flags);
 }
@@ -2314,6 +2534,7 @@
 			pr_dv_dbg("%s, provider %s registered\n",
 				__func__, provider_name);
 		dv_vf_light_reg_provider();
+		dvel_put_baseline();
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -5147,6 +5368,7 @@
 		return;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&amdv_lock, flags);
+	dvel_miss_put_locked(vf);
 	if (multi_dv_mode) {
 		if (vf && dv_inst_valid(vf->src_fmt.dv_id))
 			dv_id = vf->src_fmt.dv_id;
@@ -9708,6 +9930,7 @@
 	bool el_flag = 0;
 	bool el_halfsize_flag = 1;
 	bool el_missing = false;
+	bool dec_el_exist = false;
 	u32 w = 0xffff;
 	u32 h = 0xffff;
 	int meta_flag_bl = 1;
@@ -9826,6 +10049,7 @@
 				}
 			}
 		}
+		dec_el_exist = req.dv_enhance_exist;
 		if (debug_dolby & 1)
 			pr_dv_dbg("[inst%d vd%d]%s get %p(%d,index %d),fmt %d,aux %p %x,el %d\n",
 				     dv_id + 1,
@@ -10012,6 +10236,8 @@
 		dvel_provider = vf_get_provider_name(DVEL_RECV_NAME);
 		if (req.dv_enhance_exist && toggle_mode == 1 &&
 		    dvel_provider && !strcmp(dvel_provider, "dveldec")) {
+			if (!strcmp(dv_provider[vd_path], "dvbldec"))
+				dvel_retire_owed(dv_provider[vd_path], vf);
 			el_vf = dvel_vf_get();
 			if (el_vf &&  (el_vf->pts_us64 == vf->pts_us64 ||
 			    !(dolby_vision_flags & FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS))) {
@@ -10066,6 +10292,7 @@
 						 el_req.aux_size);
 				}
 				amdvdolby_vision_vf_add(vf, el_vf);
+				dvel_note_miss(vf, false, false);
 				el_flag = 1;
 				if (vf->width == el_vf->width)
 					el_halfsize_flag = 0;
@@ -10079,12 +10306,35 @@
 					("bl(%p-%lld) not found el(%p-%lld)\n",
 					 vf, vf->pts_us64,
 					 el_vf, el_vf->pts_us64);
+				/* Its EL is owed from now on: dvel_retire_owed()
+				 * counts this BL until it is put.
+				 */
+				if (!el_vf)
+					dvel_note_miss(vf, true, true);
 			}
 		} else if (toggle_mode == 1) {
 			if (debug_dolby & 2)
 				pr_dv_dbg("+++ get bl(%p-%lld) +++\n",
 					     vf, vf->pts_us64);
 			amdvdolby_vision_vf_add(vf, NULL);
+			/* No EL is paired with this BL. If the decoder produced one
+			 * (amdv bypassed it), that EL is owed like a miss; if the
+			 * decoder produced none, nothing is owed and the BL returns
+			 * that follow are not ELs to retire.
+			 */
+			dvel_provider = vf_get_provider_name(DVEL_RECV_NAME);
+			if (dec_el_exist && dvel_provider &&
+			    !strcmp(dvel_provider, "dveldec")) {
+				/* keep the EL queue draining while amdv bypasses it,
+				 * as the vendor comment above requires; only ELs of
+				 * BLs already toggled are retired
+				 */
+				if (!strcmp(dv_provider[vd_path], "dvbldec"))
+					dvel_retire_owed(dv_provider[vd_path], vf);
+				dvel_note_miss(vf, true, false);
+			} else {
+				dvel_note_noel(vf);
+			}
 		}
 
 		/* This picture was supposed to have an enhancement layer and did
diff -ru a/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c b/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c
--- a/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c	2026-09-21 10:31:45.000000000 -0400
+++ b/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c	2026-09-27 22:11:15.326507056 -0400
@@ -973,14 +973,21 @@
 
 	vpp_trace_vframe("video_vf_put",
 		(void *)vf, vf->type, vf->flag, 0, vsync_cnt[VPP0]);
+#ifdef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENHANCEMENT_DOLBYVISION
+	/* Not gated on is_amdv_enable(): a BL paired while amdv was on and put
+	 * while it is off (a DV mode switch, a display reset) would otherwise
+	 * strand its EL in the dv_vf table, never returned to the EL decoder.
+	 * With no table entry for this vf the call is a lookup and nothing else.
+	 * Ahead of the BL's own put so the EL put total never trails the BL's:
+	 * the EL queue realignment in amdv reads both, and a surplus of BL returns
+	 * is read as owed ELs.
+	 */
+	amdv_vf_put(vf);
+#endif
 	if (vf_put(vf, RECEIVER_NAME) < 0)
 		return -EFAULT;
 	if (IS_DI_POSTWRTIE(vf->type))
 		put_di_count++;
-#ifdef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENHANCEMENT_DOLBYVISION
-		if (is_amdv_enable())
-			amdv_vf_put(vf);
-#endif
 	video_notify_flag |= VIDEO_NOTIFY_PROVIDER_PUT;
 
 	return 0;
